cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Hydrophonic in a talk, course, exhibition, publication or derived work, please cite it as below."
title: "Hydrophonic: protein-to-music synthesizer with an audio-reactive structure visualizer"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Dietzmeyer"
    given-names: "Franz"
repository-code: "https://github.com/franzdietzmeyer/hydrophonic"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
abstract: >-
  Hydrophonic turns a protein (PDB ID, UniProt accession via AlphaFold DB, or FASTA sequence)
  into music in one of 15 styles. A composer maps secondary structure, hydropathy, charge and
  flexibility onto song form, harmony and melody, while a WebGL2 visualizer renders the fold as
  a lit cartoon and flies along the backbone to the residue being played.
keywords:
  - protein sonification
  - data sonification
  - structural biology
  - science communication
  - music generation
  - WebGL
  - Web Audio
